      "depthFt": 0.75,
      "_note": "A 12.6 x 9 in wall-hung lavatory (a cloakroom size), held 5 in clear of the door opening. Both numbers are the same trade: in a 3 ft 2 in corridor the fixtures are in series, so the basin's LENGTH is what fixes how far north the WC can sit, and its DEPTH is what blocks the doorway. Moving the old 15 x 11 in basin south without shrinking it would have bought the 5 in gap for 3.4 in of WC headroom and left the doorway just as blocked; taking it to 12.6 x 9 costs 1.5 in and unblocks 2 in as well. Anchor is the wall line."
